IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `kn-nouns`
IMPORT `kn-ch1`
IMPORT `kn-ch2`
IMPORT `kn-majority`
IMPORT `kn-ch3`

-- Mishnah Kinnim: TESTS FROM THE SOURCES.
-- Every expected value was written from a source before this file was run: the Mishnah's own numbers,
-- Bartenura's and Tiferet Yisrael's worked cases, Maimonides' example, and the cases printed by Philip
-- Reiss (Torah u-Madda Journal 9, 2000), William Gewirtz (Hakirah 30, 2021) and Eliyahu Beller (Higayon
-- 5, pp. 155-157).  Each line names its source.  Counts are of BIRDS unless the line says pairs.
-- Target compiler: main.

-- A mixture of so many designated sin offerings, designated burnt offerings and whole unassigned nests.
GIVEN ds     IS A NUMBER
      db     IS A NUMBER
      counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `Mixture`
`a test mixture of` ds db counts MEANS
    `Mixture` WITH
        `designated sin offerings`   IS ds
        `designated burnt offerings` IS db
        `unassigned obligations`     IS map `a nest of pairs` counts

-- The definition (the worst case by search) and the formula (Koppel and Reiss) for nests offered half
-- above and half below, in birds.
GIVEN counts IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the definition and the formula agree on` counts MEANS
        `the fewest offerings certainly valid in the mixture` (`nests mixed together` counts) (sum counts)
    EQUALS 2 TIMES (`the smallest majority of the nests` counts)

§ `Kinnim: tests from the sources`

§§ `1:1`

-- "A bird's sin offering is made below, a beast's above; a bird's burnt offering above, a beast's below."
#ASSERT `an offering made at this level is valid` bird `sin offering` below
#ASSERT `an offering made at this level is valid` beast `sin offering` above
#ASSERT `an offering made at this level is valid` bird `burnt offering` above
#ASSERT `an offering made at this level is valid` beast `burnt offering` below
-- "If he changed it in either, it is invalid."
#ASSERT NOT (`an offering made at this level is valid` bird `sin offering` above)
#ASSERT NOT (`an offering made at this level is valid` bird `burnt offering` below)
#ASSERT NOT (`an offering made at this level is valid` beast `sin offering` below)
#ASSERT NOT (`an offering made at this level is valid` beast `burnt offering` above)
-- "The obligation, one sin offering and one burnt offering; in vows and gifts, all are burnt offerings."
#ASSERT `sin offerings in a pair brought as` obligation EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `burnt offerings in a pair brought as` obligation EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `sin offerings in a pair brought as` vow EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `burnt offerings in a pair brought as` gift EQUALS 2
-- "What is a vow?  One who says 'upon me'.  A gift?  'This one is'."
#ASSERT `what words of dedication make the offering` `it is upon me` EQUALS vow
#ASSERT `what words of dedication make the offering` `this one is` EQUALS gift
-- "Vows ... one is answerable; gifts ... one is not."  Obligations: the text does not say.
#ASSERT `the owner must replace it if it died or was stolen` vow EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `the owner must replace it if it died or was stolen` gift EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the owner must replace it if it died or was stolen` obligation EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `1:2`

-- "A sin offering mixed with a burnt offering ... even one in ten thousand: all of them die."
#ASSERT `the most birds that may be offered as this kind from the mixture` (`a test mixture of` 1 10000 EMPTY) `sin offering` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the most birds that may be offered as this kind from the mixture` (`a test mixture of` 1 10000 EMPTY) `burnt offering` EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` (`a test mixture of` 10000 1 EMPTY) EQUALS 0
-- "A sin offering mixed with an obligation: only as many as the sin offerings in the obligation."
-- Bartenura: one sin offering among two nests, five birds: two sin offerings, and not even one burnt.
#ASSERT `the most birds that may be offered as this kind from the mixture` (`a test mixture of` 1 0 (LIST 2)) `sin offering` EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the most birds that may be offered as this kind from the mixture` (`a test mixture of` 1 0 (LIST 2)) `burnt offering` EQUALS 0
-- "Whether the obligation is many and the gift few, or the gift many and the obligation few."
#ASSERT `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` (`a test mixture of` 10 0 (LIST 2)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` (`a test mixture of` 0 1 (LIST 5)) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` (`a test mixture of` 0 7 (LIST 7)) EQUALS 7

§§ `1:3`

-- "One and one, two and two, three and three: half valid and half invalid."
#ASSERT `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 1, 1)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 2, 2)) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 3, 3)) EQUALS 6
-- "One, two, three, ten, a hundred: the fewest is valid" -- one pair (Reiss section 3: "only one pair
-- reaches the altar").  Bartenura: ten mixed with a hundred, ten nests.
#ASSERT `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100)) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 10, 100)) EQUALS 20
#ASSERT `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 1, 3)) EQUALS 2
-- Reiss section 3: three, five and twenty-seven nests: three pairs; four, six and seven: four of each.
#ASSERT `the birds of the mixture that may be offered` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 3, 5, 27)) EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `the most birds that may be offered as this kind from the mixture` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 4, 6, 7)) `burnt offering` EQUALS 4
-- The definition: one burnt offering of the hundred-and-sixteen nests is safe in every world, two are not
-- (both could be the first woman's).  Ten of ten-and-a-hundred are, eleven are not.
#ASSERT `every one of k birds offered as this kind from the mixture is valid in every possible world` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100)) `burnt offering` 1
#ASSERT NOT (`every one of k birds offered as this kind from the mixture is valid in every possible world` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100)) `burnt offering` 2)
#ASSERT `every one of k birds offered as this kind from the mixture is valid in every possible world` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 10, 100)) `sin offering` 10
#ASSERT NOT (`every one of k birds offered as this kind from the mixture is valid in every possible world` (`nests mixed together` (LIST 10, 100)) `sin offering` 11)
-- With a designated bird of the other kind present, no k at all.
#ASSERT NOT (`every one of k birds offered as this kind from the mixture is valid in every possible world` (`a test mixture of` 1 0 (LIST 2)) `burnt offering` 1)

§§ `1:4`

-- "Childbirth and childbirth ... of one reason; childbirth and discharge, of two reasons."
#ASSERT `the two obligations are of one reason` childbirth childbirth
#ASSERT NOT (`the two obligations are of one reason` childbirth discharge)
-- Rabbi Yose: bought jointly, or gave the price to the priest: he offers for whichever he wishes.
#ASSERT `the priest may assign each bird to whichever woman he wishes` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `the priest may assign each bird to whichever woman he wishes` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`the priest may assign each bird to whichever woman he wishes` FALSE FALSE)

§§ `2:1`

-- "Into the air, among the birds that must die, or one died: take a mate for the second."
#ASSERT `what follows when a bird of an unassigned pair goes` `into the air` EQUALS `take a mate for the bird left behind`
#ASSERT `what follows when a bird of an unassigned pair goes` `among birds that must die` EQUALS `take a mate for the bird left behind`
#ASSERT `what follows when a bird of an unassigned pair goes` `it died` EQUALS `take a mate for the bird left behind`
-- "Among the birds to be offered: invalid, and invalidates one corresponding to it."
#ASSERT `what follows when a bird of an unassigned pair goes` `among birds that are to be offered` EQUALS `the bird that flew is invalid and invalidates one bird where it landed`

§§ `2:2`

-- Two and two: "invalidates one in its going; ... one in its return; flew and returned, flew and
-- returned: lost nothing, for ... not fewer than two."  In nests: three, two, two.
#ASSERT `nests still offerable when two women had two nests each` 0 EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `nests still offerable when two women had two nests each` 1 EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `nests still offerable when two women had two nests each` 2 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `nests still offerable when two women had two nests each` 6 EQUALS 2

§§ `2:3`

-- The text's three tables.
#ASSERT `the nests left after round trips` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) 1 FALSE EQUALS LIST 0, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6
#ASSERT `the nests left after round trips` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) 2 FALSE EQUALS LIST 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 2, 5
#ASSERT `the nests left after round trips` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) 3 FALSE EQUALS LIST 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 4
-- "Some say: the seventh lost nothing" (Bartenura: on the third round trip; it keeps five).  The first
-- two tables are not in dispute.
#ASSERT `the nests left after round trips` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) 3 TRUE EQUALS LIST 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 5
#ASSERT `the nests left after round trips` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) 1 TRUE EQUALS LIST 0, 0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 6
#ASSERT `the nests left after round trips` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) 2 TRUE EQUALS LIST 0, 0, 0, 0, 1, 2, 5
-- "If one flew from among the birds that must die into all of them, all of them die."
#ASSERT `the nests left when a bird from among those that must die flew into every nest` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7) EQUALS LIST 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0

§§ `2:4 and 2:5`

#ASSERT `what follows a flight between an unassigned and a designated pair` `one flew from the unassigned pair to the designated pair` EQUALS `take a mate for the bird left behind`
#ASSERT `what follows a flight between an unassigned and a designated pair` `then one flew back` EQUALS `all of them die`
#ASSERT `what follows a flight between an unassigned and a designated pair` `the first flight was from the designated pair` EQUALS `all of them die`
#ASSERT `what follows a flight from the middle` `one flew from the middle to each side` EQUALS `nothing is lost`
#ASSERT `what follows a flight from the middle` `those two flew back to the middle` EQUALS `the birds in the middle die and the others are offered as the side they are on`
#ASSERT `what follows a flight from the middle` `then one flew from the middle to a side` EQUALS `all of them die`
-- "Her sin offering a turtledove and her burnt offering a young pigeon: she doubles and brings her
-- burnt offering a turtledove.  Her burnt offering a turtledove and her sin offering a young pigeon:
-- she doubles and brings her burnt offering a young pigeon."  Whichever came first (Bartenura).
#ASSERT `what she must bring again when her pair was of two species` turtledove `young pigeon` TRUE `the first view` EQUALS `bring again` `burnt offering` turtledove
#ASSERT `what she must bring again when her pair was of two species` turtledove `young pigeon` FALSE `the first view` EQUALS `bring again` `burnt offering` turtledove
#ASSERT `what she must bring again when her pair was of two species` `young pigeon` turtledove FALSE `the first view` EQUALS `bring again` `burnt offering` `young pigeon`
-- "Ben Azzai says: one goes by the first."  Burnt offering (a turtledove) first: the sin offering is
-- brought again as a turtledove (Bartenura).
#ASSERT `what she must bring again when her pair was of two species` `young pigeon` turtledove FALSE `Ben Azzai` EQUALS `bring again` `sin offering` turtledove
#ASSERT `what she must bring again when her pair was of two species` turtledove `young pigeon` TRUE `Ben Azzai` EQUALS `bring again` `burnt offering` turtledove
#ASSERT `what she must bring again when her pair was of two species` turtledove turtledove TRUE `the first view` EQUALS `nothing more`
-- "Her sin offering, and died: the heirs bring her burnt offering.  Her burnt offering, and died: the
-- heirs do not bring her sin offering."
#ASSERT `her heirs must bring the other offering of her pair` `sin offering`
#ASSERT NOT (`her heirs must bring the other offering of her pair` `burnt offering`)

§§ `3:1`

-- One and one, two and two, three and three, a priest who did not ask: half valid every way.
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 1, 1) `offered all above` EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 2, 2) `offered all below` EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 3, 3) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 1, 1) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 2

§§ `3:2: the Mishnah's case`

-- All above: half; all below: half (116 of 232).  Half and half: "the majority" -- 100 burnt offerings
-- and 100 sin offerings (Reiss section 4, after R. Zerahiah ha-Levi); 200 of 232 (Gewirtz).
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100) `offered all above` EQUALS JUST 116
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100) `offered all below` EQUALS JUST 116
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100) `offered some other number above` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The pairs to bring again together: sixteen (Reiss: "16 olot and 16 hatta'ot" invalid).
#ASSERT `the pairs the owners must bring again together` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 16

§§ `3:2: the general principle, first clause (half)`

-- Reiss section 5: 1, 3, 5, 6, 13 divide into 1+13 and 3+5+6: half valid, fourteen of each.
#ASSERT `the nests can be divided so that no woman's are both above and below` (LIST 1, 3, 5, 6, 13)
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 1, 3, 5, 6, 13) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 28
-- Tiferet Yisrael's halvable cases: 1 2 3; 1 3 4; 1 4 5; 1 2 4 5; 2 3 4 9.
#ASSERT `the nests can be divided so that no woman's are both above and below` (LIST 1, 2, 3)
#ASSERT `the nests can be divided so that no woman's are both above and below` (LIST 1, 3, 4)
#ASSERT `the nests can be divided so that no woman's are both above and below` (LIST 1, 4, 5)
#ASSERT `the nests can be divided so that no woman's are both above and below` (LIST 1, 2, 4, 5)
#ASSERT `the nests can be divided so that no woman's are both above and below` (LIST 2, 3, 4, 9)
-- Tiferet Yisrael and Reiss n. 19: 3, 4, 5 is even in total and still cannot be halved; 1, 2, 3, 10,
-- 100 cannot.  Gewirtz b): 1, 2, 3, 4 can (ten birds valid).
#ASSERT NOT (`the nests can be divided so that no woman's are both above and below` (LIST 3, 4, 5))
#ASSERT NOT (`the nests can be divided so that no woman's are both above and below` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100))
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 10

§§ `3:2: the general principle, second clause (the majority)`

-- Reiss sections 5 and 6: Sarah, Rivkah and Leah, 4, 6, 7: ten of each kind.
#ASSERT `the smallest majority of the nests` (LIST 4, 6, 7) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 4, 6, 7) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 20
-- R. Heller's counterexample (Reiss section 5): 1, 2, 3, 4, 5: eight, not Tiferet Yisrael's ten.
#ASSERT `the smallest majority of the nests` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5) EQUALS 8
-- Gewirtz: a) 2,4,6,8,10 birds: 16; d) 8,12,14 birds: 20; 2,4,8 birds: 8; against filling both containers, 8,10,10,10,14,14
-- birds: 34 (not 36) and 6,6,6,10,10 birds: 20 (not 22).
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 16
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 1, 2, 4) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 8
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 4, 5, 5, 5, 7, 7) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 34
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 3, 3, 3, 5, 5) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 20
-- Gewirtz: two nests of 2 and 4 birds: 4 of the 6.  Bartenura on 3:1: one and two, two nests valid;
-- two and three, three.  Maimonides 8:6: four birds and six: the larger (six) valid.
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 1, 2) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 4
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid when nests were mixed and the priest did not ask` (LIST 2, 3) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 6
-- Tiferet Yisrael's unhalvable cases: 1 2 4: four; 3 4 5: seven; 1 2 9: nine; 1 2 5 7: eight (pairs).
#ASSERT `the smallest majority of the nests` (LIST 1, 2, 4) EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the smallest majority of the nests` (LIST 3, 4, 5) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the smallest majority of the nests` (LIST 1, 2, 9) EQUALS 9
#ASSERT `the smallest majority of the nests` (LIST 1, 2, 5, 7) EQUALS 8
-- Beller (Higayon 5, p. 156): two, three, four: five valid by the halakhic count.
#ASSERT `the smallest majority of the nests` (LIST 2, 3, 4) EQUALS 5

§§ `3:2: the definition and the formula agree`

-- The worst case found by search over every apportionment equals Koppel's and Reiss's smallest
-- majority on every case above.
#ASSERT `the definition and the formula agree on` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100)
#ASSERT `the definition and the formula agree on` (LIST 4, 6, 7)
#ASSERT `the definition and the formula agree on` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5)
#ASSERT `the definition and the formula agree on` (LIST 1, 3, 5, 6, 13)
#ASSERT `the definition and the formula agree on` (LIST 4, 5, 5, 5, 7, 7)
#ASSERT `the definition and the formula agree on` (LIST 3, 3, 3, 5, 5)
#ASSERT `the definition and the formula agree on` (LIST 2, 3, 4)
#ASSERT `the definition and the formula agree on` (LIST 3, 4, 5)
#ASSERT `the definition and the formula agree on` (LIST 1, 2, 5, 7)
#ASSERT `the definition and the formula agree on` (LIST 2, 3)
-- Koppel's wording as Beller reports it (the larger side of the most even division) gives the same.
#ASSERT `the larger side of the most even division of the nests` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100) EQUALS 100
#ASSERT `the larger side of the most even division of the nests` (LIST 4, 6, 7) EQUALS 10
#ASSERT `the larger side of the most even division of the nests` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5) EQUALS 8
#ASSERT `the larger side of the most even division of the nests` (LIST 2, 3, 4) EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the larger side of the most even division of the nests` (LIST 1, 3, 5, 6, 13) EQUALS 14

§§ `3:2: the readings`

-- Tiferet Yisrael on 1, 2, 3, 4, 5: ten (Reiss section 5); Koppel and Reiss: eight.
#ASSERT `the valid offerings of each kind under the reading` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5) `Tiferet Yisrael` EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `the valid offerings of each kind under the reading` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5) `Koppel and Reiss` EQUALS JUST 8
-- On his own examples Tiferet Yisrael agrees with Koppel and Reiss (4,6,7: ten; 1,2,3,10,100: a hundred).
#ASSERT `the valid offerings of each kind under the reading` (LIST 4, 6, 7) `Tiferet Yisrael` EQUALS JUST 10
#ASSERT `the valid offerings of each kind under the reading` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100) `Tiferet Yisrael` EQUALS JUST 100
-- Bartenura and Maimonides: two women only.  Ten and a hundred: a hundred.  Five women: not said.
#ASSERT `the valid offerings of each kind under the reading` (LIST 10, 100) Bartenura EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `the valid offerings of each kind under the reading` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10, 100) Bartenura EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the valid offerings of each kind under the reading` (LIST 2, 3) Maimonides EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `the valid offerings of each kind under the reading` (LIST 2, 3, 4) Maimonides EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid, half above and half below, under the reading` (LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5) `Tiferet Yisrael` EQUALS JUST 20
-- Maimonides 8:7: the owner of the larger nest (six birds against four) has all her offerings count;
-- of the smaller he says nothing; of the hundred, whose birds cannot all be on one side, all count.
#ASSERT `on Maimonides' reading, all of her offerings count` 3 (LIST 2) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `on Maimonides' reading, all of her offerings count` 2 (LIST 3) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `on Maimonides' reading, all of her offerings count` 100 (LIST 1, 2, 3, 10) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Beyond the text: Beller, one and two, four birds above and two below: half valid, three.
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid for any number above, beyond the text` (LIST 1, 2) 4 EQUALS JUST 3

§§ `3:3 and 3:4`

-- A sin offering to this woman and a burnt offering to that: all above, half; all below, half; half
-- and half, both invalid.
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid in a mixture with designated birds, the priest not asking` (`a test mixture of` 1 1 EMPTY) `offered all above` EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid in a mixture with designated birds, the priest not asking` (`a test mixture of` 1 1 EMPTY) `offered all below` EQUALS JUST 1
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid in a mixture with designated birds, the priest not asking` (`a test mixture of` 1 1 EMPTY) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 0
-- A sin offering and a burnt offering, an unassigned nest and a designated nest (Bartenura: two
-- designated of each kind and one unassigned pair, six birds): half, half, and only the unassigned (two).
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid in a mixture with designated birds, the priest not asking` (`a test mixture of` 2 2 (LIST 1)) `offered all above` EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid in a mixture with designated birds, the priest not asking` (`a test mixture of` 2 2 (LIST 1)) `offered all below` EQUALS JUST 3
#ASSERT `the fewest offerings certainly valid in a mixture with designated birds, the priest not asking` (`a test mixture of` 2 2 (LIST 1)) `offered half above and half below` EQUALS JUST 2
#ASSERT `the unassigned nest counts one offering for each of the two women`

§§ `3:5`

-- "An obligation twice the sin offering: half valid" (Bartenura: two sin offerings and a burnt offering
-- left, and one sin offering fell among them: two of four).  "A sin offering twice in the obligation:
-- the number in the obligation" (two burnt offerings and a sin offering left: one).  So too a burnt
-- offering.  And 1:2's case, a whole nest of two pairs: two.
#ASSERT `the birds that may be offered when a designated bird falls among an obligation's remaining birds` `sin offering` 2 1 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the birds that may be offered when a designated bird falls among an obligation's remaining birds` `sin offering` 1 2 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the birds that may be offered when a designated bird falls among an obligation's remaining birds` `burnt offering` 1 2 EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the birds that may be offered when a designated bird falls among an obligation's remaining birds` `burnt offering` 2 1 EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the birds that may be offered when a designated bird falls among an obligation's remaining birds` `sin offering` 2 2 EQUALS 2

§§ `3:6`

-- The text's numbers.
#ASSERT `the more birds she must bring` `she did not say which birds were for her vow` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the more birds she must bring` `she did not say which birds were for her vow` TRUE FALSE EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the more birds she must bring` `she said which birds were for her vow` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the more birds she must bring` `she said which birds were for her vow` TRUE FALSE EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `the more birds she must bring` `she fixed her vow's species and forgot it` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the more birds she must bring` `she fixed her vow's species and forgot it` TRUE FALSE EQUALS 6
-- "Four for her vow, two for her obligation, and one sin offering.  Ben Azzai says: two sin offerings."
#ASSERT `the more birds she must bring` `it is not known what she gave or what the priest did` FALSE FALSE EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `the more birds she must bring` `it is not known what she gave or what the priest did` FALSE TRUE EQUALS 8
-- Bartenura's shortfalls, covered, give the text's numbers for the first two cases.
#ASSERT `the birds that make good every possible shortfall` (`the possible shortfalls, as Bartenura counts them` `she did not say which birds were for her vow` FALSE) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `the birds that make good every possible shortfall` (`the possible shortfalls, as Bartenura counts them` `she did not say which birds were for her vow` TRUE) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the birds that make good every possible shortfall` (`the possible shortfalls, as Bartenura counts them` `she said which birds were for her vow` FALSE) EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `the birds that make good every possible shortfall` (`the possible shortfalls, as Bartenura counts them` `she said which birds were for her vow` TRUE) EQUALS 4
